| Pattern       | Applicable Scenarios                                                           | Non-applicable Scenarios                                  | | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- | | Factory   | Need to create different types of objects; type is determined at runtime       | Only one type, or type is fixed and unchanging            | | Strategy  | Algorithm needs to switch at runtime; multiple interchangeable behaviors exist | Only one algorithm, or algorithm will not change          | | Observer  | One-to-many dependency; state changes need to notify multiple objects          | Simple direct calls are sufficient                        | | Singleton | A truly globally unique instance is needed, e.g., configuration management     | Objects that can be passed via dependency injection       | | Decorator | Need to dynamically add responsibilities; avoid inheritance explosion          | Responsibilities are fixed; no dynamic composition needed |
